<title>MALAYSIA: SOCCER-WORLD YOUTH CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-WORLD YOUTH CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the  world youth</p>
<p>soccer championships on Thursday:</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p>Uruguay 3 Malaysia 1 (halftime 2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Uruguay - Marcelo Zalayeta 25, 38, Hernan Lopez Mora 75</p>
<p>Malaysia - Nik Ahmad Fadly 10</p>
<p>Morocco 1 Belgium 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Morocco - Hamid Termina 78</p>
<p>Belgium - Gunter Van Handenhoven 58</p>
<p>Group C</p>
<p>France 4 South Korea 2 (3-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>France - Thierry Henry 2, 11, David Trezequet 3, 53</p>
<p>South Korea - Park Jin-sup 55, 69</p>
<p>Brazil 2 South Africa 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Adailton Martins 54, 58</p>
<p>Group E</p>
<p>Ghana 1 China 1 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ghana - Stephen Appiah 75</p>
<p>China - Li Jinyu 44</p>
<p>Ireland 2 United States 1 (2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ireland - Michael Cummins 7, Trevor Molloy 26</p>
<p>United States - Jorge Flores 39</p>
</text>
